msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note: Do not write the configuration frequently"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-note-do-not-write-the-configuration-frequently
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc
msgid ""
"Every change to a setting, whether in the web interface, via the websocket "
"or via xref:user/external-interfaces/rest-control.adoc[REST], is **written "
"permanently to the memory of the device**. On a Debian installation, the "
"files are located in `+/etc/openems.d/+`. In addition, the function "
"concerned starts working with the new values, in some cases restarting."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-note-do-not-write-the-configuration-frequently
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc
msgid ""
"Many energy management devices use **flash memory** (SD card, eMMC). Flash "
"can only withstand a limited number of write operations. **If the "
"configuration is written frequently, for example every minute by a script or "
"a home automation system, this can in the long term lead to wear, data "
"errors and ultimately failure of the storage medium.** In the worst case, "
"the system will then no longer start properly."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-note-do-not-write-the-configuration-frequently
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc
msgid "Therefore:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-note-do-not-write-the-configuration-frequently
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc
msgid ""
"Use **settings** only for rare, permanent changes, e.g. to change an "
"operating mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-note-do-not-write-the-configuration-frequently
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc
msgid ""
"Use control values for **ongoing control** (e.g. charging/discharging "
"power). They are only held in RAM, see xref:user/external-interfaces/rest-"
"control.adoc[Control via REST/JSON]."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-note-do-not-write-the-configuration-frequently
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc
msgid "Do not send unchanged values again as a setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-note-do-not-write-the-configuration-frequently
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc
msgid ""
"The xref:user/data/history-rrd4j.adoc[history] also writes regularly. The "
"more values are stored, the higher the load."
msgstr ""

